---
description: Implementation and code quality rules
alwaysApply: false
---

Inspect existing code, tests, dependencies and conventions before editing. Make focused changes. Avoid unrelated refactors and unnecessary abstractions.

For non-trivial work, state a plan and acceptance criteria before implementation. Validate inputs at trust boundaries. Enforce authorisation server-side. Use migrations for schema changes. Consider transactions, concurrency and idempotency for state changes.

Run relevant tests, lint and build checks where available. Report exact commands and results; never claim checks passed if they were not run. Update docs and task status when applicable.
